.SH INTERACTIVE COMMANDS
Typed at the composer; Enter runs a command only on an exact name or alias
match with the palette marker on its own row (otherwise Enter walks the list
and Tab picks). avail: idle | live | any.
.TP
.B /help, /h \fI[keys|commands|reload]\fR
keys by context, commands with one\-liners, per\-terminal notes (any)
.TP
.B /new, /nw
end the session; the next prompt starts a new one here (idle)
.TP
.B /resume, /r, /sessions, /continue \fI[id|title]\fR
pick a session to continue, or continue <id|title> (idle)
.TP
.B /rename \fI<title>\fR
set the session title (≤ 60 chars) (any)
.TP
.B /steer \fI<text>\fR
queue a directive for the next step (= Enter while live) (live)
.TP
.B /unsteer
take the newest queued steer back (= Up on the first row) (live)
.TP
.B /pause \fI[now] [<target>]\fR
stop after the step in flight commits (= Esc); `now` interrupts, a target asks
a peer (any)
.TP
.B /abort
stop the run now (= Esc Esc); the step in flight is discarded (live)
.TP
.B /undo, /u \fI[n]\fR
restore the files a step changed (verify\-before\-write) (idle)
.TP
.B /rewind, /rw \fI[step]\fR
pick a step; undo last…n, then files / plan+window / both (idle)
.TP
.B /diff, /d \fI[step] [\-\-full] [\-\-all]\fR
numstat block of the run's changes (\-\-full opens the pager) (any)
.TP
.B /plan, /pl
append the plan ledger block (any)
.TP
.B /decisions, /dc \fI[n] [stage]\fR
append the last n decision rows (default 12) (any)
.TP
.B /why, /w \fI<ref|digit>\fR
why Jev decided as it did (s7.risk.plan_mismatch, risk.plan_mismatch, or a
pane digit) (any)
.TP
.B /calibration
reliability bins, ECE and near\-threshold counts (idle)
.TP
.B /jev, /j
decider model, drift, questions, latency p50/p95, Jev cost (any)
.TP
.B /cost, /c
run and session spend, per\-step cost, pending caps (any)
.TP
.B /budget, /b \fI[spend\-cap|session\-spend\-cap|max\-steps|max\-wall|max\-replans <v>]\fR
show or set caps (spend\-cap, session\-spend\-cap, max\-steps, max\-wall,
max\-replans) (any)
.TP
.B /model, /ml \fI[id]\fR
generator model for the next run only (any)
.TP
.B /provider \fI[anthropic|openrouter|openai|gemini|xai|fireworks|meta]\fR
generator provider for the next run only (any)
.TP
.B /mode, /m \fI[jev\-only|jev\-on|jev\-off|llm\-jev]\fR
engine mode: show, or set for the next run (any)
.TP
.B /llm \fI<on|off>\fR
Jev + LLM on (= /mode jev\-on) or off (= /mode jev\-only) (any)
.TP
.B /config, /cf
masked settings table with sources and the effective session cap (any)
.TP
.B /login, /l
re\-enter a missing or rejected API key (applies to the next run) (any)
.TP
.B /logout \fI[generator|jev]\fR
remove a saved key from the config file (any)
.TP
.B /trust
reopen the workspace trust gate (idle)
.TP
.B /theme, /t \fI<dark|light|daltonized|ansi>\fR
colour theme for new items and the dynamic region (any)
.TP
.B /panel, /p \fI[d|p|t|s|a|off|full]\fR
Jev panel: toggle, open a tab (d|p|t|s|a), collapse (off) or expand (full)
(any)
.TP
.B /transcript, /tr \fI[compact|full]\fR
transcript view: compact (one line per step) or full (every stage line) (any)
.TP
.B /copy, /cp \fI[last|proposal|diff|draft|conversation]\fR
copy the last turn, proposal, diff, draft or conversation (redacted) (any)
.TP
.B /export \fI[file]\fR
write the session transcripts to a file (idle)
.TP
.B /status, /s
run id, session id, step/max, stage, sandbox, workspace, git, stop reason,
lock (any)
.TP
.B /errors
append recent warnings and errors; acknowledges !n (any)
.TP
.B /report
write a redacted support bundle under ~/.jevcode/reports/ (idle)
.TP
.B /history \fIclear\fR
clear the prompt history (after y/N) (any)
.TP
.B /editor
edit the draft in $VISUAL / $EDITOR (= Ctrl+G) (any)
.TP
.B /exit, /q, /quit
leave (exit 0; confirms first while a run is live) (any)
.TP
.B /fullscreen
pin the header at the top of the screen (persists ui.renderer; needs a
relaunch) (any)
.TP
.B /scrollback
print the transcript to the primary screen for copy and find (any)
.TP
.B /peers
other jevcode instances working in this workspace · /who shows what
each is doing (any)
.TP
.B /ui \fIreset\fR
ui maintenance: reset re\-enables panes that failed to render (any)
.TP
.B /who \fI[\-\-all]\fR
every jevcode session on this repo, with what each is doing (any)
.TP
.B /inbox \fI[\-\-all]\fR
unread messages from other sessions, newest first (any)
.TP
.B /tell \fI<target> <text>\fR
send one session a message (any)
.TP
.B /headsup \fI<text>\fR
broadcast what you are about to touch to every live session here (any)
.TP
.B /request \fI<target> pause|end|steer [<text>]\fR
ask a session to pause, end or take a steer — it answers y/n (any)
.TP
.B /end \fI[now] [<target>]\fR
end this session — /resume afterwards needs \-\-force (any)
.TP
.B /context
what the generator sees this step, and what it costs (any)
.TP
.B /compact
fold the history now instead of waiting for the next trigger (live)
.TP
.B /split \fI[auto|ask|off]\fR
the split policy for the next step (any)
.TP
.B /agents
the agent tree — opens and focuses the `a` pane tab (Alt+A) (any)
.TP
.B /agent \fI<slug> pause|resume|steer|budget|land|kick|drop|diff [args]\fR
one verb against one agent, by slug (any)
.TP
.B /land \fI[<slug>]\fR
land a finished agent's work into the dock (idle)
.TP
.B /spawn \fI<role> <glob> [task]\fR
one extra agent against the live manifest (live)
.TP
.B /import, /imp \fI[\-\-dry\-run] [<source>]\fR
import memory, commands and settings from the other coding agents on this
machine (idle)
.TP
.B /memory, /mem \fI[list|show|add|forget|reload] [<text>]\fR
the project and user memory this run reads (any)
.SH KEYS
.SS Global
.TP
.B Ctrl+C
idle: press twice within 1.5 s to exit; live: abort the run (with a draft:
clear it)
.TP
.B Ctrl+D
empty draft: press twice within 800 ms to exit (live: choose abort\-and\-exit
or stay); with text: delete forward
.TP
.B Esc
idle: Esc Esc opens the rewind/steer menu; text: Esc Esc clears the draft;
live: pause, Esc Esc aborts (a reply with no tool call yet: stop it); review:
decline
.TP
.B ?, F1
append the help block to the transcript
.TP
.B Ctrl+O
append the last step's decision details and recent warnings; acknowledges !n
.TP
.B Ctrl+L
repaint the dynamic region (erase\-lines + rewrite, never a clear)
.TP
.B Ctrl+Z
suspend to the shell (fg resumes and repaints)
.TP
.B ]
next pane tab (d → p → t → s, + a while delegating);
opens a collapsed panel
.TP
.B [
previous pane tab; opens a collapsed panel
.TP
.B Alt+A
focus the agents tab so its keys resolve (Esc unfocuses); refused with a
non\-empty draft
.TP
.B Alt+J
toggle the Jev panel between the collapsed strip and the open 6\-row form (=
/panel, /panel off)
.TP
.B Alt+Shift+J
open the Jev panel in its full 12\-row form (= /panel full)
.TP
.B Alt+D
open the panel on the decisions tab; a second press on the same tab collapses
it (= /panel d)
.TP
.B Alt+P
open the panel on the plan tab; a second press collapses it (= /panel p)
.TP
.B Alt+T
open the panel on the timeline tab; a second press collapses it (= /panel t)
.TP
.B Alt+S
open the panel on the synth tab; a second press collapses it (= /panel s)
.SS Composer
.TP
.B Enter
submit: task, follow\-up, steer while live, /command, review note
.TP
.B Ctrl+J, Alt+Enter, Shift+Enter
insert a newline
.TP
.B Ctrl+A, Home
start of the logical line
.TP
.B Ctrl+E, End
end of the logical line
.TP
.B Ctrl+B, Left
move one grapheme left
.TP
.B Ctrl+F, Right
move one grapheme right; at the end of the text accepts the ghost completion
.TP
.B Alt+B, Ctrl+Left
word left (Intl.Segmenter word; / \- _ . separate)
.TP
.B Alt+F, Ctrl+Right
word right
.TP
.B Ctrl+K
kill to the end of the line → kill ring
.TP
.B Ctrl+U
kill to the start of the line → kill ring
.TP
.B Ctrl+W, Alt+Backspace
kill the word before the cursor (unix\-word\-rubout)
.TP
.B Alt+Del, Ctrl+Del
kill the word after the cursor
.TP
.B Ctrl+Y
yank the newest kill
.TP
.B Alt+Y
rotate the kill ring (right after a yank)
.TP
.B Ctrl+T
transpose the two graphemes around the cursor
.TP
.B Ctrl+_
undo (100 snapshots)
.TP
.B Ctrl+^
redo
.TP
.B Backspace
delete back; a paste chip is removed whole
.TP
.B Del
delete forward; a paste chip is removed whole
.TP
.B Up
move up one visual row; on the first row: history prev; with steers queued and
an empty draft: take the newest steer back
.TP
.B Down
move down one visual row; on the last row: history next
.TP
.B Ctrl+P
history prev (always)
.TP
.B Ctrl+N
history next (always)
.TP
.B Ctrl+R
reverse\-incremental history search (Ctrl+R older, Ctrl+S newer, Tab/→
accept, Enter accept + submit, Esc restore; Ctrl+A widens to all workspaces)
.TP
.B Tab
completion: palette, mention or argument — accept or cycle; never focus
.TP
.B Shift+Tab
cycle completion backwards
.TP
.B /
open the command palette pre\-filled with /
.TP
.B @
open the @ file mention popup over the candidate list
.TP
.B Ctrl+G
edit the draft in $VISUAL / $EDITOR (refused while the draft holds a secret)
.SS Review box
.TP
.B Y
approve the proposed action once
.TP
.B N
decline
.TP
.B D
decline with a note (the composer row becomes the note field)
.TP
.B E
expand / collapse the preview
.TP
.B W
then 1–5 within 1.5 s: append the /why block for that dimension (5 =
matches_intent)
.TP
.B Ctrl+C
empty draft: abort the run (the rejected confirm() is the decline); with a
draft: clear the draft, the box stays
.SS Session picker
.TP
.B Up, Ctrl+P
previous row
.TP
.B Down, Ctrl+N
next row
.TP
.B PgUp
page up
.TP
.B PgDn
page down
.TP
.B Enter
continue / resume the highlighted row
.TP
.B Tab
accept the row and keep filtering
.TP
.B Space
preview the highlighted run (plan counts, spend, stop)
.TP
.B Ctrl+A
toggle all workspaces
.TP
.B Ctrl+R
rename the highlighted session inline
.TP
.B X
then y: move the run directory to ~/.jevcode/trash/ (never rm \-rf)
.TP
.B Esc
close the picker
.TP
.B R
resume by replaying the paused proposal (only when it is still replayable)
.TP
.B F
resume with a fresh step instead of the paused proposal
.TP
.B D
diff the workspace since the pause
.TP
.B W
who else is live on this repo right now
.SS Agents tab
.TP
.B Enter
attach to the highlighted agent read\-only (its transcript tails into the
pane)
.TP
.B P
pause the highlighted agent at its next step (= /agent <slug> pause)
.TP
.B T
steer the highlighted agent (the composer row becomes the steer field)
.TP
.B +
raise the highlighted agent's cap (= /agent <slug> budget)
.TP
.B D
the highlighted agent's diff against the base (= /agent <slug> diff)
.TP
.B K
kick the highlighted agent once (= /agent <slug> kick)
.TP
.B X X
then x again: drop the agent — its uncommitted diff is lost, which is
why it takes two keys
.TP
.B L
land the highlighted agent into the dock (= /agent <slug> land)
.SS Palette
.TP
.B Up, Ctrl+P
previous row
.TP
.B Down, Ctrl+N
next row
.TP
.B PgUp
page up
.TP
.B PgDn
page down
.TP
.B Tab
put the highlighted row in the draft
.TP
.B Enter
run the armed draft; otherwise move to the next row
.TP
.B Esc
close (the draft is kept; the token is remembered so / stays closed while it
is unchanged)
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
complete / generator_done / answered (a reply-only agent run); /exit, Ctrl\-D
\(mu)2, Ctrl\-C \(mu)2 idle (leaving is not a failure)
.TP
.B 1
uncaught error or an escalated render fault
.TP
.B 2
configuration or usage error at launch; first\-call 401/403; unpriced model
without \-\-allow\-unpriced
.TP
.B 3
checkpoint degraded and stopped (state.json not resumable)
.TP
.B 4
a budget stop (max_steps, wall_time, spend_cap, max_replans, token_cap),
replan_stop, impossible, human_pause, stuck (the agent loop detector)
.TP
.B 5
API failure after retries; provider spend limit
.TP
.B 6
sandbox or path abort
.TP
.B 129
SIGHUP / EIO
.TP
.B 130
Ctrl\-C \(mu)2 while a run is live (one\-shot) or an external SIGINT
.TP
.B 143
SIGTERM
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.jevcode/runs/<run\-id>/
run directory: run.json, state.json, steps.jsonl, transcript.log, jevcode.log,
pre/, post/, ui.json
.TP
.I ~/.jevcode/sessions/index.jsonl
the session index
.TP
.I ~/.jevcode/history.jsonl
composer history (redacted, 1,000 entries)
.TP
.I ~/.jevcode/trust.json
workspace trust decisions
.TP
.I ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:\-~/.config}/jevcode/config.json
configuration and stored keys (mode 0600)
.TP
.I ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:\-~/.config}/jevcode/keybindings.json
key rebindings (namespace:action → key, chord or "none")
.TP
.I \&./jevcode.json, ./.env
per\-workspace configuration and dotenv fallback
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TYPESAFE_API_KEY, OPENROUTER_API_KEY, JEV_API_KEY, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
decider (Jev) and generator keys; jev\-only needs one Jev key
.TP
.B JEVCODE_MODE, JEV_PROVIDER
engine mode (jev\-only | jev\-on | jev\-off | llm\-jev | agent; default
llm\-jev) and Jev provider (auto | typesafe | openrouter)
.TP
.B JEVCODE_HOME
root of runs/, sessions/ and history (default ~/.jevcode)
.TP
.B JEVCODE_CONFIG, JEVCODE_KEYBINDINGS
configuration and keybindings file paths
.TP
.B JEVCODE_SPEND_CAP_USD, JEVCODE_SESSION_SPEND_CAP_USD
run and session spend caps
.TP
.B JEVCODE_THEME, JEVCODE_FPS, JEVCODE_ASCII, JEVCODE_SCREEN_READER, JEVCODE_REDUCED_MOTION
UI settings (flag > env > file > default)
.TP
.B JEVCODE_LOG, JEVCODE_LOG_LEVEL, JEVCODE_TRACE
log file and level (keys never appear in logs)
.TP
.B NO_COLOR, FORCE_COLOR
colour control
.TP
.B CI, TERM=dumb
select the plain renderer
.SH SEE ALSO
docs/TUI-DESIGN.md, docs/KEYS.md, docs/COMMANDS.md in the source tree.
